{{/*
The work identity (§6.5, ADR 0003), read from the single 1Password item that carries it.
This is the only place the item and its fields are named, and it serves the five surfaces
that render from them: the `includeIf` in ~/.gitconfig, ~/.config/git/config-work, the
work line in ~/.config/git/allowed_signers, the ssh `Host` block, and ~/.ssh/id_work.pub.

The item's own name and its vault appear here, in a public tree, so neither names the
client either. Nothing in the item is cryptographically secret — the signing key is a
public key and the host is a public DNS name. What is kept out of the tree is the client
relationship, which is why the unit is the whole identity and never half of it.

It hands its caller JSON built by `toJson` rather than text the caller parses, so a field
holding a quote is escaped by the encoder instead of ending the value early. Written by
hand, the same partial breaks on a name like `A "Quoted" Name` — and it would break at
apply time, on the one machine that renders the populated branch.

Every call site guards on `op` being on the path, so this template is reached only on a
machine that has 1Password. It does not guard a second time: a template that refused here
would be the refusal the gate already owns (§2).
*/ -}}
{{- $item := "op://Private/work-identity" -}}
{{- dict
      "host" (onepasswordRead (printf "%s/host" $item))
      "name" (onepasswordRead (printf "%s/name" $item))
      "email" (onepasswordRead (printf "%s/email" $item))
      "key" (onepasswordRead (printf "%s/public_key" $item))
  | toJson -}}
